  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R1 and R2 establish that moment tensor potentials can be used for atomistic simulation of a closely related BCC refractory HEA and that SRO can materially affect its behavior. R3 and R15 further show consequential SRO in another BCC refractory HEA, while R5 and R14 provide only broad support for finite-temperature electronic or electronic-structure contributions in other HEAs. However, none of the records describes liquid-phase MTP training against the DFT phase-space distribution, free-energy perturbation as a replacement for thermodynamic integration, variance-controlled MTP-to-DFT corrections, or electronic and SRO corrections to melting temperatures. The literature therefore points toward ML potentials and relevant physical corrections, but constructing the specific MTP–FEP melting workflow would require a substantial new idea."
